{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds","id":1186334,"title":"Extinct Breeds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-15T09:11:37-08:00","id":1186334,"title":"Extinct Breeds","content":"I was super excited when Shattered Dreams came out - and it was pretty cool and all - but then a bit dissapointed<br /> There were other Breeds, long ago others existed, who either died out long ago when their animal Kin were extinct or were actively destroyed by other Fera. In most cases, their cultures as well as their duty to Gaia has been forgotten and neglected since their demise - and Shattered Dreams forgot to mention them<br /> Maybe somebody can help me to fill the blanks , morsel of knwoledge hidden in some old books, and such I never read, who knows!<br /> So lets see:<br /> <br /> - <b>Insect Races </b>- okay pretty easy. Breed Book: Ananasi and Rokea is a good information source for these guys (kinda). But their time was before the Dragon Kings or the lived alongside the Kings? The Dragon Kings missed the whole Insect Wars? Looked the other way? Never knew about it?<br /> <br /> The Insect were the easy as I said, but there are---- others:<br /> <br /> - After the Age of Kings, <b>Ammonite </b><b>shifters</b> (who were at war with the Rokea) and <b>bristlecreepers</b> went extinct along with their Kin (Breed Book: Mokol\u00e9 p.21) - First things first, what the hell is a &quot;bristlecreeper&quot;? No, really. What is it? Any info about these guys?<br /> - <b>Qyrall</b> (the shapshifter Breed of Anemone Shifters, breed of Qyrl and they almost wiped out the Rokea - Breed Book: Rokea p.44) - The poor shark folks are not the most loved shifters by the players or Storytellers, yet their history is rich and quite bloody (no pun intended) , the Sharks it seems iced three other shifter-breeds, the Ammonite shifters, the bristlescreepers and the Qyrall. Not even the Garou managed to exterminate three breeds! Then again the Sharks had couple of million years to do do this. This undersea genocide went unnoticed too... ? Is there any information about this war under the waves? Or anything about their possible revival? After all Qyrl is one of the most active Wyrm....ish (not really a bad girl, but this is another mater) spirit around and her tentacles are deep in Humanity (no Hentai references please, it was just an experession) and interested in their science!<br /> <br /> And there are some... honorable mentions:<br /> - The Corax speak of a race of <b>were-megatheriums</b> that were slaughtered in the War of Rage. (Breed Book: Corax p.22)<br /> - Rumours among the Nagah tell of a <b>breed of humans that could assume the shape of freshwater fishes</b>, who went extinct in the War of Rage. (Breed Book: Nagah p.46)<br /> - The Shadow Lords remember a breed of <b>werefalcons</b> that were destroyed in the War of Rage. (Tribe Book: Shadow Lords Revised p.13)<br /> - The Fianna remember tribes of <b>wereotters</b> and <b>wereeagles</b> that fell beneath their claws in the War of Rage (Tribe Book: Fianna p.15)<br /> - Rumours among the Beast Courts tell of breeds of sapient <b>shapeshifting orangutans</b> in the indonesian rainforests ( Players Guide to the Changing Breeds, p. 27)<br /> <br /> So, while most of these are tales and legends mentioned only once, they are considered &quot;canon&quot;? Is there any source material about these unknown and extinct exotic breeds? (Or any plans to do so, like in the Shattered Dreams?^^)<br /> <br /> Anyhow, any and every help and scrap of information about these long gone Breeds are apriciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 02-15-2018, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T09:49:44-08:00","id":1186339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds#post1186334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First things first, what the hell is a &quot;bristlecreeper&quot;? No, really. What is it? Any info about these guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to guess, based on ammonites and Qyral being cephalopod shifters (?), I'd say sea urchins, sea cucumbers, and starfish?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":1813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","user":"grimjaws","date":". 02-15-2018, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T10:13:46-08:00","id":1186347,"title":"","content":"Just one little question - how can there be were creatures before there are humans? Because the most basic point about a were creature is that they change shape from [species] to human.<br /> <br /> So what did ammonites et al change shape to?<br /> <br /> Or is the mythology completely at odds with the science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 02-15-2018, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T11:29:19-08:00","id":1186367,"title":"","content":"Possibly a mythology at odds with science, I mean World of Darkness the idea that parts of history might be significantly less than accurate as baseline humans understand it is not unheard of. That or you had weird incidents where you had prehistoric crabs turning into half crabs half squid horror shows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T11:38:17-08:00","id":1186369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186347#post1186347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one little question - how can there be were creatures before there are humans? Because the most basic point about a were creature is that they change shape from [species] to human.<br /> <br /> So what did ammonites et al change shape to?<br /> <br /> Or is the mythology completely at odds with the science?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well from the Qyrall description from the Rokea breedbook is:<br /> <br /> &quot;You know what an anemone is, right? There was a time when anemones were not rooted to one spot the way they are now. Instead, they had a snail-like foot under them, and they oozed across the ocean floor. They were also much bigger than they are now, and their arms were strong enough to hold and poision a Rokea, if we got thatclose. These creatures- called the Qyrall, after their mother - used sand and theri own ooze to build up fortresses underwater, using knowledge that Qyrl stole from C'et. They would ride the leviathans and use Qyrl's gifts of stealth to block out the massive brutes' presence until they were right on top of a slew, then change in to an<b> almost-humanoid</b> shape to do battle&quot;<br /> <br /> There were were-creatures waaay before the humans, just before humans never had a homid form, just animal and war-form (humanoid-animal, aka. anthro). The homid part came after the humans. (or/and in Shattered Dreams the Drachid,that bridged the three Dragon King line and was a possibility to the Rokea and Ananasi, but they never - or ever - really used it for obvious reasons )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T13:20:09-08:00","id":1186388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186339#post1186339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to guess, based on ammonites and Qyral being cephalopod shifters (?), I'd say sea urchins, sea cucumbers, and starfish?</div> </div> </div> </div>Way off on that one, since they weren't mentioned in the Rokea book. According to Wolaru in the Mokole Breedbook, they might have been mammals, inasmuch as she described them as covered in fur and giving live birth (kind of paraphrasing on the second part there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T15:46:24-08:00","id":1186444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186388#post1186388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Way off on that one, since they weren't mentioned in the Rokea book. According to Wolaru in the Mokole Breedbook, they might have been mammals, inasmuch as she described them as covered in fur and giving live birth (kind of paraphrasing on the second part there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Some kind of porcupine then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 02-16-2018, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T20:56:04-08:00","id":1186533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186444#post1186444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some kind of procupine then?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems far too contemporary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T02:02:49-08:00","id":1186585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186388#post1186388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Way off on that one, since they weren't mentioned in the Rokea book. According to Wolaru in the Mokole Breedbook, they might have been mammals, inasmuch as she described them as covered in fur and giving live birth (kind of paraphrasing on the second part there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was aware of that, but never really knew what kind of little mammal they were (and actually how they died out? It is a bit hard to immagine the Rokea to wander to the land to hunt down little mammal-shifters just for fun. And their time was after the Dragon Kings'... so... blame the Ananasi, maybe? Dunno...)<br /> Hoped someone know, what was a &quot;<b>bristlecreeper&quot; </b>^^<br /> <br /> To be honest I tought it was some early mammal, like the Eomia (<b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eomaia\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eomaia</a> ) </b>or something along the line<b>, </b>maybe some spiritual ancestor of the Ratling and other mammalian shifters, like the Khara were the Bastet ancestor (used to at least) and the new Changing Breed book (honestly I don't remember wich book) suggest there was a bridge between the Khara and the Mokol\u00e9, some common ancestor of the reptiles and mammals and the Kara had some connection to the Mnesis of the Mokol\u00e9 (they removed things that shoudn't be remembered, while the Mokol\u00e9 gathered the things to remember... pretty cool concept)<br /> <br /> Anyhow we almost solved the &quot;Bristlecreeper&quot; mystery (some official help would be cool tho' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Word of God/Wod )<br /> But there are others <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 02-16-2018, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T04:51:18-08:00","id":1186612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186388#post1186388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Way off on that one, since they weren't mentioned in the Rokea book. According to Wolaru in the Mokole Breedbook, they might have been mammals, inasmuch as she described them as covered in fur and giving live birth (kind of paraphrasing on the second part there).</div> </div> </div> </div>That will teach me for not digging back through the breedbooks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T18:47:38-08:00","id":1186896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186347#post1186347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one little question - how can there be were creatures before there are humans? Because the most basic point about a were creature is that they change shape from [species] to human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It's ridiculous. Now I don't mind the idea that before humanity there was some other kind of lifeform which protected Gaia. But they weren't werecreatures. It's also why I've always thought the Mokole as ridiculous as weredinosaurs. I've never used them in my chronicles, but they're in the background if I ever need them - except that they are &quot;merely&quot; werecrocodiles.<br /> <br /> Most of the extended backstory in the Werewolf setting has gotten so weird that I ignore almost all of it in favor of my own interpretation of Garou/Fera history and the Time Before Man.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T20:36:51-08:00","id":1186920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186896#post1186896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. It's ridiculous. Now I don't mind the idea that before humanity there was some other kind of lifeform which protected Gaia. But they weren't werecreatures. It's also why I've always thought the Mokole as ridiculous as weredinosaurs. I've never used them in my chronicles, but they're in the background if I ever need them - except that they are &quot;merely&quot; werecrocodiles.<br /> <br /> Most of the extended backstory in the Werewolf setting has gotten so weird that I ignore almost all of it in favor of my own interpretation of Garou/Fera history and the Time Before Man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mokole are werereptiles(except snakes!) with a really wierd middleform.<br /> <br /> Corax are weredinosaurs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T21:03:28-08:00","id":1186927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186896#post1186896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. It's ridiculous. Now I don't mind the idea that before humanity there was some other kind of lifeform which protected Gaia. But they weren't werecreatures. It's also why I've always thought the Mokole as ridiculous as weredinosaurs. I've never used them in my chronicles, but they're in the background if I ever need them - except that they are &quot;merely&quot; werecrocodiles.<br /> <br /> Most of the extended backstory in the Werewolf setting has gotten so weird that I ignore almost all of it in favor of my own interpretation of Garou/Fera history and the Time Before Man.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For me, personally since Shattered Dreams outlined how the Kings didn't have the same animal forms as modern mokole, nor the same homid/drachid form...to me they weren't technically mokole back then. More they evolved into the Mokole. <br /> <br /> So as Lian said...werereptiles (except snakes) with weird middle forms (and hey I like said weird middle form)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T21:13:41-08:00","id":1186929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186334-extinct-breeds?p=1186927#post1186927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For me, personally since Shattered Dreams outlined how the Kings didn't have the same animal forms as modern mokole, nor the same homid/drachid form...to me they weren't technically mokole back then. More they evolved into the Mokole.<br /> <br /> So as Lian said...werereptiles (except snakes) with weird middle forms (and hey I like said weird middle form)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the weird middle forms because.. they aren't real. They are living history as the memory of Gaia given form. Now you get wierd shit like the Zhong Lung but that just means we are missing some pieces of History.<br /> <br /> Also I prefer the old Mokole book and the Etherite book which matches up with it which had all these species that rose and fell. The Mokole just get to be the Memory recording for this time period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T01:12:09-08:00","id":1186978,"title":"","content":"ooh I didn't know there was a reference to Insect breeds in Rokea! I was going to make a log called Noah's ark for shifter breeds in classic world of darkness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T06:25:33-08:00","id":1187027,"title":"","content":"Guys... do you realize, Humanity is a pretty recent addition on Gaia - on the Earth, right?<br /> She nedded defenders before some celver ape fell down from a tree... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (Garou lifespan was even closer to wolf lifespan before the mass interbreeding with Humans)<br /> <br /> Back to the original topic, any more extinct breeds we missed?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2